00:00:39.001 --> 00:00:42.950
It was pretty funny from someone who said,
oh wait.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.399
Oh, it was from you.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:46.670
Just you emailed in.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.670
Yeah.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.500
You had a bunch of interesting things where
you explained that like the head, the family

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.190
he's saying is the oldest family isn't, and
he's got the lineages wrong.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.130
And the funny thing is, like any normal person
would listen to that and know it doesn't make

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.130
any sense.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.870
But then as you did, when you actually look
into the specifics, it makes even less sense.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.500
Speaker 2: Right.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.030
Now, I wanted to ask you a question.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.340
I've been called a monster for this.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.799
I shower with my glasses on.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:18.320
Am I a monster for that?

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.670
Speaker 1: That I have never heard of that
ever.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.119
I've never heard of anyone doing that.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:26.140
I will sometimes shower with my contact on
and I know that that's controversial.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.710
And people will say, Oh, sir, you could get
a crazy infection from that.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:36.520
I mean, I've been doing it off and on for,
you know, 20 years, but I have never heard

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.630
of anyone showering with glasses on.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.770
How don't they get all steamed up?

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.500
Speaker 2: Well, yeah, but then I'll just,
you know, wipe them off with my towel and

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.500
then I'll be fine.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.930
Speaker 1: Wait, you're bringing a towel into
the shower?

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.830
Speaker 2: Well, it'll be hanging out outside
of it.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.420
And then I can just, you know, poke my head
out and wash them off for a second.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.490
Speaker 1: So how many times do you have to
do that during your typical shower?

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.060
Speaker 2: Oh, like four or five.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.560
Speaker 1: So you're telling me that what
you do is you wear glasses during the shower,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.500
hang a towel outside, and then five times
per shower, lean out to wipe them.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.500
Speaker 2: That's correct.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.989
Speaker 1: Wouldn't it be easier just to take
them off?

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:14.499
Speaker 2: Um.

00:02:14.499 --> 00:02:15.510
Probably, yeah.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.769
Do it all my life, you know.

00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:19.189
Speaker 1: What, are you, nearsighted?

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:20.889
Speaker 2: I'm far sighted.

00:02:20.889 --> 00:02:23.180
Speaker 1: Oh, so these are reading glasses?

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.180
Yes.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.269
Oh, interesting.

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:27.579
And you need you feel like you need those
to shower.

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:32.900
Speaker 2: I mean, I don't want to like slip
on something or fall or whatever, so I kind

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.760
of like feel more comfortable with them on.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.650
Speaker 1: Well, listen, safety is our number
one priority, if that's what you need to feel

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.650
safe.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.650
But it is certainly unorthodox.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.000
I will I will leave it there, Roy.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.099
Speaker 2: All right.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:44.099
Thank you for your assessment.

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:45.920
Speaker 1: You're still allowed in the audience,
though.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.920
It's not that crazy.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.920
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:48.920
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:49.920
All right.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.920
Roy from South Jersey.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:51.920
Wow.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:52.920
Showering with glasses on.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.920
I've never heard of it.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:54.920
Never.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.920
Never heard of it.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.920
Very interesting.

